{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-g1-reviewer-fable-32","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:be2cd19d5dfaf5bcdd56","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The declared independent-unit column is accession_id, and the CSV contains exactly 16 data rows with 16 distinct accession IDs (FSB-101 through FSB-116); no ID appears on more than one row.","observed_value":{"n_data_rows":16,"n_unique_accession_ids":16,"duplicate_ids":[]},"source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":11,"end_line":11,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: accession_id"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"FSB-101,Dryopteris filix-mas,Craigmore Glen,2021,100,52,56"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":17,"end_line":17,"quoted_text":"FSB-116,Pteridium aquilinum,Harrow Common,2024,100,34,45"}]},{"description":"The workflow explicitly guards against repeated independent-unit entry: it aborts if any accession_id occurs on more than one row before any statistics are computed.","observed_value":"SystemExit raised on duplicate accession codes","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":30,"end_line":32,"quoted_text":"codes = [row[UNIT_COL] for row in rows]\n    if len(set(codes)) != len(codes):\n        raise SystemExit(\"every accession must appear on exactly one row\")"}]},{"description":"The selected statistical procedure is a paired t-test on one within-row difference per accession, so the number of analysed observations (16) equals the number of independent units, and the reported degrees of freedom equal n - 1 = 15.","observed_value":{"n_differences":16,"df_reported":15},"source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":50,"end_line":57,"quoted_text":"gain = cryo - freezer\n\n    n = int(gain.size)\n    df = n - 1\n    mean_gain = float(np.mean(gain))\n    sd_gain = float(np.std(gain, ddof=1))\n    se_gain = sd_gain / float(np.sqrt(n))\n    tstat, pval = stats.ttest_rel(cryo, freezer)"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":34,"end_line":34,"quoted_text":"Paired t-test: t(15) = 5.333, p < 0.0001 (two-sided)."}]},{"description":"Recomputation from the raw CSV confirms the reported selected result: the 16 within-accession differences (cryo minus freezer) are 4, 12, 1, 18, 7, 2, 10, 1, 16, 5, 8, 19, 1, 9, 4, 11, giving mean 8.00 pp, SD 6.00, SE 1.50, t = 8.00/1.50 = 5.333 on 15 df, 95% CI 4.80 to 11.20 pp, and Wilcoxon W = 0 since every difference is positive. All match the report, so the reported statistics correspond to exactly one entry per independent unit.","observed_value":{"mean_diff_pp":8,"sd_diff_pp":6,"se_diff_pp":1.5,"t":5.333,"df":15,"ci_pp":[4.8,11.2],"wilcoxon_W":0},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":28,"end_line":31,"quoted_text":"| mean paired difference (pp) | 8.00 |\n| SD of paired differences (pp) | 6.00 |\n| standard error of the mean difference (pp) | 1.50 |\n| 95% CI for the mean difference (pp) | 4.80 to 11.20 |"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":37,"end_line":37,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Paired t-test on 16 accession-level differences (one difference per accession): cryogenic storage at -196 C raised 18-month spore germination by 8.00 percentage points relative to -20 C storage (95% CI 4.80 to 11.20 pp; t(15) = 5.333, p < 0.0001, two-sided)."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"Each accession contributes two measurements (freezer and cryo percentages), which could superficially look like the same unit entering the analysis twice; however, the two values sit in one row as a matched pair and the procedure analyses their within-row difference, which is the correct paired treatment rather than row-independent double entry.","observed_value":"two matched columns per row, reduced to one difference per row","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":23,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"The two\npercentages inside a row are matched measurements on the same lot, which is why\nthe analysis works with the within-row difference instead of treating the two\ncolumns as independent samples."}]},{"description":"A few genera appear on two rows (Dryopteris on FSB-101 and FSB-113, Athyrium on FSB-102 and FSB-114, Asplenium on FSB-104 and FSB-112), which might be mistaken for repeated units; but the stated independent unit is the accession, and the description confirms each accession came from its own maternal plant at its own site with no subsampling or re-measurement, so these are distinct independent units, not repeated entries of one unit.","observed_value":{"genera_on_two_rows":["Dryopteris","Athyrium","Asplenium"]},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"FSB-101,Dryopteris filix-mas,Craigmore Glen,2021,100,52,56"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":14,"end_line":14,"quoted_text":"FSB-113,Dryopteris affinis,Redlaw Spinney,2023,100,63,64"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":22,"end_line":23,"quoted_text":"Accessions came from different sites and were never subsampled or re-measured,\nso no accession is represented twice and no two rows share a source lot."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to establish the issue by (1) scanning all 16 CSV rows for any repeated accession_id value (none found; 16 unique IDs), (2) checking whether the workflow expands, duplicates, or pools rows before testing so that one accession could enter the test more than once (it does not: it reads rows once, computes one difference per row, and passes exactly those arrays to stats.ttest_rel and stats.wilcoxon), (3) checking whether reported sample size or degrees of freedom exceed the number of independent units, which would betray hidden repeated entries (n = 16 and df = 15 match 16 units exactly), and (4) recomputing the mean difference, SD, SE, t statistic, CI, and Wilcoxon statistic from the raw data, all of which reproduce the reported values under one entry per accession. I also considered whether spores_scored = 100 per plate constitutes repeated unit entry, but individual spores are never entered as rows; only the accession-level percentage is analysed. No path to demonstrating the issue class survived these checks.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}